  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "Consider the function \\(f(x)=\\frac{x^n(1-x)^n}{n!}\\), where \\(n\\ge1\\) is a fixed integer. Let \\(f^{(k)}\\) denote the \\(k\\)-th derivative of \\(f\\). Which of the following is true for all \\(k\\ge1\\)?",
  "options": {
    "A": "\\(f^{(k)}(0)\\) and \\(f^{(k)}(1)\\) are integers",
    "B": "\\(f^{(k)}(0)\\) is an integer, but not \\(f^{(k)}(1)\\)",
    "C": "\\(f^{(k)}(1)\\) is an integer, but not \\(f^{(k)}(0)\\)",
    "D": "Neither \\(f^{(k)}(1)\\) nor \\(f^{(k)}(0)\\) is an integer."
  },
  "answer": "A",
